NAME
    ls - list directory contents

SYNOPSIS
    ls [-l] [-a] [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Lists the entries in <path> (default: the current directory), sorted by
    name (case-insensitive). Files print plain; directories with a trailing /.
    The default layout is multi-column; dotfiles are hidden.

OPTIONS
    -l    Long form, one entry per line: type (d/-), size, and modified
          YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM. The time is shown where the filesystem records
          one (FAT32 does; others show a dash).
    -a    Include dotfiles, and the . and .. entries.

SEE ALSO
    tree, cat, stat
